§§ `s 261 -- the time for a claim`

#ASSERT `By when must I claim compensation` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I claim compensation` (`d` 10 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 20 9 2026
-- An "awareness" before the injury does not move the date.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim compensation` (`d` 10 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 5 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 7 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I claim compensation` (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026

-- Arguments: injury, aware later, day aware, first claim, reasonable cause, serious and permanent disablement, insurer
-- accepted the late claim, Authority approved.
-- The last day of the 6 months, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 10 7 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 11 7 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 11 7 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With reasonable cause: the last day of the 3 years, the day after, and the day after with serious and permanent disablement.
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 10 1 2029) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 11 1 2029) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 11 1 2029) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The insurer accepts a late claim: within 3 years it may; after, only with the Authority's approval.
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 11 1 2029) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 11 1 2029) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 261(6): injured 10 January 2024, first aware 1 June 2026: the 6 months run to 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the time limit stop me` (`d` 10 1 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 2 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 267, 268 -- provisional weekly payments`

#ASSERT `By when must my provisional weekly payments start` (`d` 28 12 2025) EQUALS `d` 4 1 2026

-- Initial notification 1 March 2026: the 7 days run to 8 March.
-- Arguments: notification, reasonable excuse, payments started, day started, excuse notice given, day of it, today.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 8 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty was kept`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 9 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty was not kept`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 5 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty is still open`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 8 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty is still open`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 9 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty was not kept`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 6 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty was kept`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty was not kept`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 8 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty is still open`
-- A written "excuse" the Guidelines do not recognise does not answer s 267.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer started my payments in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 6 3 2026) (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `the duty was not kept`

